#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059715 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059528 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bc170fa-a70e-55af-8f3e-f4ea07431e30" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector From Position Vectors and then Computing its Magnitude"}] :question/id #uuid "d4ad6011-24a4-5642-997f-dcc4e807224f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4298" :question/problem "Let $A(1,3)$ and $B(2,-2)$. Find $\\mid \\overrightarrow{AB} \\mid$.\n\n![](images/f9/f95ee3c5c81750d97019d910350e4c78f0962baa682c834928450a451691145a.png)" :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\nOA^(→) = a = i + 3j,; OB^(→) = b = 2i - 2j\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB^(→) &= OB^(→) - OA^(→) \\\\\n&= b - a \\\\\n&= (2i - 2j) - (i + 3j) \\\\\n&= i - 5j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid AB^(→) \\mid &= \\sqrt{1^{2} + (-5)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{1 + 25} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{26}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bc170fa-a70e-55af-8f3e-f4ea07431e30" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050136}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501415 :question-generator/id #uuid "76b43aba-c2a9-5fb6-93b1-151df1f6da0b" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186059715.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060127 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bc170fa-a70e-55af-8f3e-f4ea07431e30" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector From Position Vectors and then Computing its Magnitude"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fa76cd1-659d-5a5b-8d30-aa37db4db6b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057121} {:answer/id #uuid "c207c803-b1ce-5924-b942-d55d34b0a896" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057122} {:answer/id #uuid "fb4bdbac-dae8-512d-9f28-a6d1ca641844" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057123} {:answer/id #uuid "5c31b652-4b6c-5d88-8099-aa3b8dbea173" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057124} {:answer/id #uuid "70729c42-11e6-5309-82bb-19226d272451" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057125}] :answer-field/id #uuid "21f89363-a985-51cc-946e-14f2aa27f506" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057120}] :question/id #uuid "6a56ae9f-24f2-57fe-8fdd-fdcdaeb8e97e" :question/math-academy-id "q-18051" :question/problem "![](images/2c/2c1f9580f07d06af7ec900ee63c95872e06f459107e64cf1b5117d928efdab22.png)\n\nLet $A(-4, 1)$ and $B(3, 0)$. Find $\\mid AB^(→) \\mid$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060128 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bc170fa-a70e-55af-8f3e-f4ea07431e30" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector From Position Vectors and then Computing its Magnitude"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "859a4033-c7be-5ff5-af88-1823e959391b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057127} {:answer/id #uuid "ad6482c5-d423-5cfa-b5c4-60571c0a06c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{23}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057128} {:answer/id #uuid "e1496379-7a78-53b1-8d89-c51305772b95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057129} {:answer/id #uuid "e7ded905-451e-5e8d-87f6-0bff47652269" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057130} {:answer/id #uuid "4818a873-c410-58c3-9fa9-c071285aa2cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057131}] :answer-field/id #uuid "60525c6f-c622-5ce0-b076-32a8f28ba4a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057126}] :question/id #uuid "1c261405-1fb7-5f8f-992e-8a8c19696484" :question/math-academy-id "q-18052" :question/problem "![](images/0d/0d92a4d7b9c59b0d6bc8ffec9926bcf189c9bbe808c5bed7a02d6ab09bcebcd0.png)\n\nLet $P(-2, 2)$ and $Q(3, 3)$. Find $\\mid PQ^(→) \\mid$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233366 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bc170fa-a70e-55af-8f3e-f4ea07431e30" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector From Position Vectors and then Computing its Magnitude"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "02dcce11-c60f-5753-ba12-d8ce046f2ae1" :question/math-academy-id "q-125118" :question/problem "![](images/f3/f35a3ad730621023ec86e5727588fc86083ee500b3a72c55ab2808bd290019e9.png)\n\nLet $P(1,2)$ and $Q(-2,1).$ Find $|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}|.$" :question/worked-solution "We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OP}=p=i+2j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OQ}=q=-2i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =q-p \\\\  & =(-2i+j)-(i+2j) \\\\  & =-3i-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233596 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bc170fa-a70e-55af-8f3e-f4ea07431e30" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector From Position Vectors and then Computing its Magnitude"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f6f7008d-b645-50b0-a00b-9cf227ed2ff3" :question/math-academy-id "q-18049" :question/problem "![](images/1a/1a250499768a91e3e225a05d141e42d7ed89168ba82c5560777f64b8b29fac4a.png)\n\nLet $C(-1,3)$ and $D(1,-2).$ Find $|\\overset{\\to }{CD}|.$" :question/worked-solution "We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OC}=c=-i+3j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OD}=d=i-2j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{CD}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CD} & =\\overset{\\to }{OD}-\\overset{\\to }{OC} \\\\  & =d-c \\\\  & =(i-2j)-(-i+3j) \\\\  & =2i-5j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{CD}| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233598 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bc170fa-a70e-55af-8f3e-f4ea07431e30" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector From Position Vectors and then Computing its Magnitude"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c14ed0ed-41e3-5534-b77e-503efe93d887" :question/math-academy-id "q-18055" :question/problem "![](images/1e/1e3e9c336bf85cf0f19b2326f12c5fd986fee5b0aae65b8d79257ea234efee13.png)\n\nPoints $P$ and $Q$ are shown in the picture above. Find $|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}|.$" :question/worked-solution "From the picture, we obtain $P(1,1)$ and $Q(2,3).$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OP}=p=i+j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OQ}=q=2i+3j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =q-p \\\\  & =(2i+3j)-(i+j) \\\\  & =i+2j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501385 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bc170fa-a70e-55af-8f3e-f4ea07431e30" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector From Position Vectors and then Computing its Magnitude"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0445042e-54ee-545e-a3f8-732df318f4f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501380} {:answer/id #uuid "0490c650-33f4-5c2c-b521-fe9b1e566ec1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501381} {:answer/id #uuid "6ddf7c05-e687-5019-8cfe-0f4da5991c7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501395} {:answer/id #uuid "8a0025cb-b64b-5f84-97d4-564a7a574582" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501397} {:answer/id #uuid "c88fd2c8-d986-5a88-8aac-ff25f7704891" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0490c650-33f4-5c2c-b521-fe9b1e566ec1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501381} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c461d70-6214-536b-9b0f-2806ac3e820b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501386}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "351db615-bec0-5fbb-9adf-d33132b902d9" :question/problem "![](images/07/07a59129f6186959fa9ebad8b924177a81910a3d25c2f292169c41474df99a31.png)\n\nLet $A(-12, 3)$ and $B(9, 0)$. Find $|\\overrightarrow{AB}|$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OA} &= a = - 12 i + 3 j, \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{OB} &= b = 9 i.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{AB} &= \\overrightarrow{OB} - \\overrightarrow{OA} \\\\\n&= b - a \\\\\n&= (9 i) - (- 12 i + 3 j) \\\\\n&= 21 i - 3 j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\overrightarrow{AB}| &= \\sqrt{(21)^{2} + (-3)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{441 + 9} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{450} \\\\\n&= 15 \\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501390 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bc170fa-a70e-55af-8f3e-f4ea07431e30" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector From Position Vectors and then Computing its Magnitude"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1064156b-f30e-55b2-b6f0-e825bc55e1e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501382} {:answer/id #uuid "22689487-5be7-57f4-83d8-1de65d9b4694" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501384} {:answer/id #uuid "643ef294-255a-50c2-b361-7fb11bf24717" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501393} {:answer/id #uuid "c82c134e-3f2c-5916-9411-d5e7b2847411" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501404} {:answer/id #uuid "f609e524-19c0-530c-a969-08f856f8f9e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c82c134e-3f2c-5916-9411-d5e7b2847411" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501404} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3672b93-4679-5491-bb12-4ccb62ec0b4e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501400}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "51236f62-ba5d-5c78-8128-0c42c6d77d9b" :question/problem "![](images/56/5682cc802577e4dd43f42e03bfc829658fc96ca83a15422aa079fe2b43258a0c.png)\n\nLet $A(-8, 2)$ and $B(6, 0)$. Find $|\\overrightarrow{AB}|$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OA} &= a = - 8 i + 2 j, \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{OB} &= b = 6 i.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{AB} &= \\overrightarrow{OB} - \\overrightarrow{OA} \\\\\n&= b - a \\\\\n&= (6 i) - (- 8 i + 2 j) \\\\\n&= 14 i - 2 j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\overrightarrow{AB}| &= \\sqrt{(14)^{2} + (-2)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{196 + 4} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{200} \\\\\n&= 10 \\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501391 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bc170fa-a70e-55af-8f3e-f4ea07431e30" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector From Position Vectors and then Computing its Magnitude"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4555636f-851f-5e9a-97d4-f0c927f479bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501388} {:answer/id #uuid "684fb4dc-3f86-5814-8b54-f899578ebd2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501394} {:answer/id #uuid "c1702806-4afa-5e76-baef-2d46830762f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501403} {:answer/id #uuid "c9fac228-4948-536a-82ec-632379bd0a8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501406} {:answer/id #uuid "f61881ec-1910-5308-9caa-62794e33d7f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1702806-4afa-5e76-baef-2d46830762f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501403} :answer-field/id #uuid "b49bb760-a1d5-54eb-84a1-6966067cef0b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501401}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5b1e6461-4662-5ed4-8cde-319bf158b165" :question/problem "![](images/57/57fd993fac384d9dd76399aa35eec0d9113afeb3c1d24c0a5349d7b4b99df4f1.png)\n\nLet $A(-16, 4)$ and $B(12, 0)$. Find $|\\overrightarrow{AB}|$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OA} &= a = - 16 i + 4 j, \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{OB} &= b = 12 i.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{AB} &= \\overrightarrow{OB} - \\overrightarrow{OA} \\\\\n&= b - a \\\\\n&= (12 i) - (- 16 i + 4 j) \\\\\n&= 28 i - 4 j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\overrightarrow{AB}| &= \\sqrt{(28)^{2} + (-4)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{784 + 16} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{800} \\\\\n&= 20 \\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501407 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bc170fa-a70e-55af-8f3e-f4ea07431e30" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector From Position Vectors and then Computing its Magnitude"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70508e9b-a14a-5a98-8e92-1e7ad5d853c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501396} {:answer/id #uuid "8d049bb8-f5e4-5c04-829f-a53cafde9397" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501398} {:answer/id #uuid "a0451aba-8b5c-5281-ac81-2b22e276ad68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501399} {:answer/id #uuid "df4172c0-8628-54c0-81a3-e9013141b07a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501409} {:answer/id #uuid "f95e5d75-a09f-5293-b330-062df6b3f507" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{23}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df4172c0-8628-54c0-81a3-e9013141b07a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501409} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d4df1b5-ef4c-5db5-95a8-06e66305be52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d8e7cd39-a979-5900-aba6-00ca0310cc42" :question/problem "![](images/d7/d7b3f6503172aeab9c4554ffac492a9aab8c16e9ce14f5c552cd1d89dcaa3c66.png)\n\nLet $P(-4, 4)$ and $Q(6, 6)$. Find $|\\overrightarrow{PQ}|$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &= p = - 4 i + 4 j, \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{OQ} &= q = 6 i + 6 j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{PQ} &= \\overrightarrow{OQ} - \\overrightarrow{OP} \\\\\n&= q - p \\\\\n&= (6 i + 6 j) - (- 4 i + 4 j) \\\\\n&= 10 i + 2 j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\overrightarrow{PQ}| &= \\sqrt{(10)^{2} + (2)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{100 + 4} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{104} \\\\\n&= 2 \\sqrt{26}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501414 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bc170fa-a70e-55af-8f3e-f4ea07431e30" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector From Position Vectors and then Computing its Magnitude"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1da9c0a6-14cc-517f-a698-c8a70ee46bb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501383} {:answer/id #uuid "45e58fef-c1c7-52df-807b-c1a8f907804d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501389} {:answer/id #uuid "5bdee396-6d9f-5bbe-8378-a50d04de0635" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501392} {:answer/id #uuid "df2d382e-5a80-52bc-a649-14e4acf7e481" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\sqrt{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501408} {:answer/id #uuid "fd3387cd-5801-5797-af72-00603e84116c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\sqrt{23}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df2d382e-5a80-52bc-a649-14e4acf7e481" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\sqrt{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501408} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7666596-5028-5069-996f-ad5e72c1af9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501402}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ff8c4899-ff23-5168-90d9-e8d647d7f269" :question/problem "![](images/6b/6bd80d88ece15997923e5860ff1328dea542c2950c9e4399eba6a5e872070f18.png)\n\nLet $P(-6, 6)$ and $Q(9, 9)$. Find $|\\overrightarrow{PQ}|$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OP} &= p = - 6 i + 6 j, \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{OQ} &= q = 9 i + 9 j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{PQ} &= \\overrightarrow{OQ} - \\overrightarrow{OP} \\\\\n&= q - p \\\\\n&= (9 i + 9 j) - (- 6 i + 6 j) \\\\\n&= 15 i + 3 j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\overrightarrow{PQ}| &= \\sqrt{(15)^{2} + (3)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{225 + 9} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{234} \\\\\n&= 3 \\sqrt{26}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector From Position Vectors and then Computing its Magnitude"}]}
